<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eberhard IV, Count of Württemberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1388">1388</a>–<a href="/years/1419">1419</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Eberhard the Younger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eberhard IV (1388–1419), called the Younger, was Count of Württemberg from 1417. In 1397, as a child, he was betrothed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henriette-of-montbeliard">Henriette of Montbéliard</a>, heiress of the County of Montbéliard, and their marriage brought Montbéliard to the House of Württemberg, which held it until 1793. He died after only two years of rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eberhard-iv-count-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="Eberhard IV, Count of Württemberg" width="320" height="527" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Strasbourg workshop · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:28W%C3%BCrttemberg_und_M%C3%B6mpelgard_Eberhard_IV_T%C3%BCbingen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
